// src/v4/lens/application.dag
//
// Scope: lens-application surface — how a user attaches a lens to a program section (declaration / module / expression scope) with configurable enforcement. THE opt-in-depth mechanism + user-defined-dimensions surface + the ONLY advisory→fail-closed bridge. Referenced by report.dag/synthesis.dag's apply_lens(Enforce) — this file is its substrate home.
// Anchor: THESIS:95-101 (user-defined dimensions) + THESIS:307-321 (audience duality / opt-in depth) + r3-structure.md:40 (v3 T-Lens-Application-Surface precedent)
//
// Owns:
//   - EnforcedApplication<Output, Budget> (lens, section, budget, severity, span)
//   - IntrospectApplication<Output> (lens, section, span; no Budget — advisory)
//   - SectionRef = DeclarationScope | NodeScope (disjoint sum; where the lens attaches)
//   - apply_lens(lens, section, config) — the user-facing surface
//   - THE single advisory→fail-closed bridge: Enforce { } converts a lens's
//     Set<Report> into fail-closed Diagnostics (per std/report.dag discipline);
//     no other path from advisory to blocking exists
//
// QRY-1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — "language queries" ARE
// user-defined dimensions; this file is their home. A query is a
// USER-DEFINED LENS (the same `Node -> Set<Match>` / `Witness` shape as
// every lens; THESIS §1.5/95-101 — "a user writes a lens in .dag … the
// compiler validates every program against it using the same mechanism
// as built-in dimensions"). Properties, by construction:
//   - LANGUAGE-AGNOSTIC by the B2-OMNI Node pivot: a query is written
//     against `Node`, so ONE query runs over every ingested language
//     (Rust/Python/Verilog/SQL/…) with no per-language rewrite — O(1)
//     per language, the same O(N+M) argument as B2-OMNI. This is a free
//     consequence and is asserted here (was folklore, now contract).
//   - Composes DERIVED facts, not just syntax: a query may read other
//     lenses' outputs (effects/complexity/parallelism/…), strictly more
//     than text/AST tools.
//   - Introspective READ by default (`IntrospectApplication` — you run a
//     query to SEE); `Enforce` optional (a query becomes a fail-closed
//     custom gate/policy). Same uniform UX as parallelism/complexity.
//   - A query RESULT is itself a `Node` (bounded kernel — NO new output
//     carrier: a structured collection of matched Node-refs + their
//     InferredFacts). Fail-closed/no-engine: empty match = empty set (a
//     fact); unmodeled concept = Diagnostic, never a guess.
//   - NON-MOVE (binding): there is NO `query.dag` / query subsystem. A
//     query IS a lens; a query feature would be parallel authority with
//     the lens shape = the feature-creep the closed system forbids. STOP.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/witness.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/report.dag
//   - lens/*.dag: the lenses being applied (complexity/cost/synthesis/...)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-23
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.lens.application

